Bugfix: Prevent deleting intact repository config during aborted v2 upgrade rollback

When upgrading a repository from version 1 to 2, an aborted migration
attempted contingency rollback by unconditionally removing the configuration
file before re-saving it. On atomic backends (such as local filesystems),
the original configuration was intact, and deleting it during a failed rollback
left the repository unopenable. Restic now conditions config pre-removal
on whether the backend lacks atomic replacement.

